WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.235
Step 6: backout triggers
are set before each ring,

2
00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:08.091
for example sign-in failures above the
baseline, help desk calls above the

3
00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:13.425
threshold, a mission application unreachable,
or TLS failures above one percent.

4
00:00:13.425 --> 00:00:18.385
When one fires, apply Step 3's rollback
with its approved hash, do its manual

5
00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:23.263
steps in order, and collect again so
the evidence shows the state after it.

6
00:00:23.263 --> 00:00:25.637
In Stage 1, rehearse it once.

7
00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:30.462
Step 7 records every run of the stage
and checks the stage's evidence.

8
00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:34.267
In the fixture, every file matches,
five records form a chain,

9
00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.762
and each step the test stage
needs has a passing record.

10
00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:42.240
Production also needs the telemetry
step, with CISA telemetry agreed.
